[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3879748634","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695#issuecomment-3879748634","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695","id":3879748634,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87nQEQa","user":{"login":"jeffdaily","id":904248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNDI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/904248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffdaily","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffdaily/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-10T17:44:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T17:44:03Z","body":"CC @IvanKobzarev https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/136260","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3879748634/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3983249680","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695#issuecomment-3983249680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695","id":3983249680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87ta5EQ","user":{"login":"krastogi-in","id":224517637,"node_id":"U_kgDODWHeBQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224517637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in","html_url":"https://github.com/krastogi-in","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T09:42:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T09:42:34Z","body":"@eellison , @xmfan , @mlazos , The RCA is that there is not synchronize_event supported in inductor and dynamo is calling call_method instead of call _function on even synchronization . This will result in race condition to sync host and device. I think we can support synchornize_event in inductor lowering by: \n\n`make_fallback(torch.ops.streams.synchronize_event.default)`\n\n and add custom ops in  dynamo streams:\n\n`@custom_op(\"streams::synchronize_event\", mutates_args=())\ndef synchronize_event(event_index: int) -> None:\n    event = _get_event_by_index(event_index)\n    event.synchronize()\n\n\n@synchronize_event.register_fake\ndef _(\n    event_index: int,\n) -> None:\n    pass\n\n\nhas_side_effect(torch.ops.streams.synchronize_event.default)`\n\nIn EventVariableTracker support that using: \n\n```\n        elif name == \"synchronize\":\n            tx.output.create_proxy(\n                \"call_function\", torch.ops.streams.synchronize_event,\n                (self.user_object_index,),\n                {},\n            )\n```\nThis adds sync in events. Please let me know your opinion and the I can create PR for the same.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3983249680/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3999930117","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695#issuecomment-3999930117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695","id":3999930117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87uahcF","user":{"login":"morrison-turnansky","id":214027003,"node_id":"U_kgDODMHK-w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214027003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky","html_url":"https://github.com/morrison-turnansky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T19:59:03Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T20:09:14Z","body":"The general idea seems fine. However, I am a bit concerned about using has_side_effect. The docstring explicitly says:\n  \n```python\nNOTE: For new operators, please do not add to this set!\n  Instead, consider using the effects system via\n  torch.library._register_effectful_op() for operators.\n```\n\nDoes your strategy work for this? @krastogi-in  \n\n\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3999930117/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4022725992","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695#issuecomment-4022725992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695","id":4022725992,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87vxe1o","user":{"login":"krastogi-in","id":224517637,"node_id":"U_kgDODWHeBQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224517637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in","html_url":"https://github.com/krastogi-in","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krastogi-in/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T10:26:08Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T10:26:08Z","body":"> The general idea seems fine. However, I am a bit concerned about using has_side_effect. The docstring explicitly says:\n> \n> NOTE: For new operators, please do not add to this set!\n>   Instead, consider using the effects system via\n>   torch.library._register_effectful_op() for operators.\n> Does your strategy work for this? [@krastogi-in](https://github.com/krastogi-in)\n\n@morrison-turnansky , the strategy works here however reordering happens of operations and this out record and synchronize in top rather than after device_put operations hence we need a check in reorder_for_locally to prevent such reordering when index put is there and source and destination device are different.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4022725992/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4024244227","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695#issuecomment-4024244227","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/174695","id":4024244227,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87v3RgD","user":{"login":"morrison-turnansky","id":214027003,"node_id":"U_kgDODMHK-w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214027003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky","html_url":"https://github.com/morrison-turnansky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/morrison-turnansky/repos","events_u